From e842bbc63fda41ebea395e23194d916f9c7ccab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fzdark build <build@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:19:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] interface: give the already-connected options distinct
 control IDs

Connecting to a second server while one is already open raises the
"Already connected" dialog, which offers "new tab" or "abort previous",
plus an "always perform this action" checkbox. In dark mode all three of
those controls are invisible: the dialog reserves the space, and the
message and the OK/Cancel buttons draw, but the option area comes out
blank and the choices cannot be read.

They are not being drawn in a colour that clashes. Nothing paints them at
all, which is why the area is one perfectly uniform colour with no
anti-aliasing.

wx makes wxRadioButton and wxCheckBox owner-drawn whenever dark mode is
active (src/msw/radiobut.cpp and src/msw/checkbox.cpp both call
MSWMakeOwnerDrawn(wxMSWDarkMode::IsActive() || m_hasFgCol)). An
owner-drawn control is not painted by Windows at all; it sends
WM_DRAWITEM to its parent and draws only if the parent handles it. In
wx that handler is wxWindowMSW::MSWOnDrawItem, which resolves the
control to draw with wxWindowMSW::FindItem(id), and that lookup matches
on the control ID alone. wxControl::MSWFindItem ignores the HWND
completely, so the first child of the dialog with a matching ID wins,
regardless of which control is actually asking to be drawn.

Every control in this dialog was created with nullID, which is
wxID_HIGHEST. The static bitmap holding the question icon is created
first, so it answered WM_DRAWITEM for all three option controls. Being a
static control it has no MSWOnDraw override and inherits the base
wxWindowBase::MSWOnDraw, which returns false. False tells Windows the
request was not handled, and since the controls are owner-drawn Windows
does not fall back to drawing them itself, so they stayed blank.

That is also why this is invisible in light mode: the controls are only
owner-drawn under dark mode, and in light mode Windows draws them
directly and the ID collision never comes into play.

Give the three option controls distinct IDs so the lookup can only
resolve to themselves. conditionaldialog.cpp already gives its checkbox
wxID_HIGHEST + 1 for the same reason, so this follows the existing
convention rather than inventing one.

The IDs are never used for events here: the dialog is not event-driven
and the result is read straight from the control pointers after
ShowModal returns, so giving them real IDs changes no behaviour beyond
making them paint.

Verified against wxWidgets 3.3.3 and FileZilla 3.71.1.
---
 src/interface/Mainfrm.cpp | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/interface/Mainfrm.cpp b/src/interface/Mainfrm.cpp
index 15ec10c..be1e6b4 100644
--- a/src/interface/Mainfrm.cpp
+++ b/src/interface/Mainfrm.cpp
@@ -2110,14 +2110,20 @@ bool CMainFrame::ConnectToSite(Site & data, Bookmark const& bookmark, CState* pS
 
 			main->Add(new wxStaticText(&dlg, nullID, _("FileZilla is already connected to a server.")));
 
-			auto newtab = new wxRadioButton(&dlg, nullID, _("Establish connection in a new tab"), wxDefaultPosition, wxDefaultSize, wxRB_GROUP);
+			// These need distinct IDs, not nullID. wx resolves WM_DRAWITEM for
+			// owner-drawn controls by ID alone, and dark mode makes radio buttons
+			// and check boxes owner-drawn; sharing an ID with the icon above means
+			// the icon wins the lookup, and a static control answering the draw
+			// request leaves the options unpainted. See conditionaldialog.cpp,
+			// which gives its checkbox a real ID for the same reason.
+			auto newtab = new wxRadioButton(&dlg, wxID_HIGHEST + 1, _("Establish connection in a new tab"), wxDefaultPosition, wxDefaultSize, wxRB_GROUP);
 			main->Add(newtab);
-			auto oldtab = new wxRadioButton(&dlg, nullID, _("&Abort previous connection and connect in current tab"));
+			auto oldtab = new wxRadioButton(&dlg, wxID_HIGHEST + 2, _("&Abort previous connection and connect in current tab"));
 			main->Add(oldtab);
 
 			main->AddSpacer(0);
 
-			auto remember = new wxCheckBox(&dlg, nullID, _("Al&ways perform this action"));
+			auto remember = new wxCheckBox(&dlg, wxID_HIGHEST + 3, _("Al&ways perform this action"));
 			main->Add(remember);
 
 			if (action != 0) {
